# OSLO Release 1 — Heroku process model (DL-054: app runs NATIVE on Heroku;
# only the backing services — Supabase/Neo4j/Redis — are dockerised elsewhere).
#
# web   — the FastAPI transport (uvicorn). Heroku injects $PORT; bind 0.0.0.0.
#         Durable LangGraph runs execute INLINE on this dyno through the Supabase-
#         Postgres checkpointer (backend/orchestration/runner.submit_trigger is
#         called synchronously from the command routers), so a single web dyno is
#         sufficient for R1. The in-process coalescing guard
#         (orchestration/runner.CoalescingGuard) is per-process — correct for a
#         single web dyno.
#
# A dedicated `worker` dyno is NOT enabled for R1. It becomes required only when
# durable runs move off the request path AND the deployment scales to >1 dyno —
# that needs the Redis cross-dyno coalescing guard flagged as the Phase-II-A
# follow-up in orchestration/runner.py and api/deps.py. Enabling it is a scaling
# change (owner-approved), not part of this staging-binding slice.
web: uvicorn backend.api.app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port ${PORT:-8000}

# release — runs once per deploy, BEFORE the new web dyno starts. Migrations are
# a gated pipeline step (Deployment Governance §5), forward-only and additive;
# canonical stores stay append-only. `supabase db push` applies pending
# migrations in timestamp order against $SUPABASE_DB_URL (the platform secret
# store injects it per environment — never committed). Commented OUT by default:
# on Heroku the Supabase CLI is not on the buildpack, and migration application
# is owner-gated for Staging/Production. Document + run it via the runbook
# instead (code/docs/DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md). Re-enable only once the deploy
# image carries the Supabase CLI and the owner authorises pipeline migration.
# release: supabase db push --db-url "$SUPABASE_DB_URL"
